{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"title":"Sending batches"},{"anchor":"Encoding-a-batch","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"],"title":"Encoding a batch"},{"anchor":"Splitting-a-batch-into-requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord"],"title":"Splitting a batch into requests"},{"anchor":"Retrying-a-vendors-own-statuses","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidTransientStatus"],"title":"Retrying a vendor’s own statuses"},{"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"title":"Waiting between attempts"},{"anchor":"Sending-requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"],"title":"Sending requests"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"externalID":"HTTPDestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yours. It sends with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. So is one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answered with a status the encoder lists in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which every encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declares: empty for most servers, or each other failure its vendor answers to a request worth"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sending again, such as Aptabase’s 418 for a slow upload. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its requests. So is a request still undelivered at its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder sets for a vendor that misdates or ignores old events: the destination checks it on its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now:"},{"type":"text","text":" clock before every attempt and sends nothing more once it has passed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, give the destination a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"text":"); for PostHog,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"make it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken:host:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Amplitude, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mixpanel, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"text":");","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.segment(writeKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:)"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"text":"); for Google Analytics 4, from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},{"text":"); for Snowplow, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SnowplowEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeck, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:)"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"},{"text":"); for Matomo, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MatomoEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Heap, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.heap(appID:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeapEncoding"},{"text":"); for Aptabase, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AptabaseEncoding"},{"text":"). To read events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inside the app or in a test, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"text":") instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    static let transientStatuses: Set<TransientStatus> = []","","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<Never> {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        let body = EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","        return BatchRequests(requests: [EncodedRequest(body: body, recordIDs: batch.map(\\.id))], skippedRecords: [])","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"How long ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" wai